# Update Mods From Collection SOP

## Purpose
This SOP describes the procedure for updating all mods from the bin^2 B42.13 collection in the project-zomboid-mods repository.

## Preconditions
- User has internet access to fetch Steam Workshop data
- User has write access to the project-zomboid-mods repository
- Current working directory is the project-zomboid-mods folder

## Procedure

### Step 1: Fetch Collection Data
```
IF WebFetch is available THEN
    Navigate to "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3624259825"
    Extract the complete list of mods from the collection page
    COUNT the total number of mods in the collection
    SAVE the mod list for comparison
ELSE
    Display "WebFetch tool not available - cannot proceed"
    EXIT the procedure
END
```

### Step 2: Compare with Current Records
```
OPEN "collection/README.md"
READ the current mod count from the file
IF current_count < fetched_count THEN
    CALCULATE difference = fetched_count - current_count
    DISPLAY "New mods detected: " + difference
    IDENTIFY the new mods from the fetched list
ELSE
    DISPLAY "No new mods found"
END
```

### Step 3: Update Collection README
```
IF new mods exist THEN
    FOR EACH new mod in new_mods DO
        ADD the mod to the appropriate category in collection/README.md
    END
END

EDIT "collection/README.md"
    REPLACE old version number with new version number
    REPLACE old mod count with new mod count
    REPLACE old date with current date
END
```

### Step 4: Update Main README
```
EDIT "README.md"
    REPLACE "模组数量（XXX个" with new count
    REPLACE "最近更新：XXXX年X月X日" with current date
END
```

### Step 5: Update Changelog
```
OPEN "collection/updates.md"
IF file contains "## [YYYY-MM-DD]" for today THEN
    APPEND new mods to the existing section
ELSE
    CREATE new section "## [current_date]"
    ADD new mods list to the new section
END
```

### Step 6: Commit Changes
```
IF user requests commit THEN
    RUN "git status" to see all changed files
    RUN "git diff" to review changes
    ADD relevant files to staging
    CREATE commit with message describing the update
END
```

## Postconditions
- All documentation files reflect the current state of the collection
- Changes are ready to be committed (if requested)

## Example Output
```
Fetching collection data from Steam Workshop...
Found 123 mods in collection (previously 101)
22 new mods detected
Updating documentation files...
Update complete!
```
